# Lesson 3: Project Structure & Database Setup

As our application grows, keeping everything in [main.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/main.py) becomes unmanageable. We need a scalable structure. We also need a database to store our users and documents permanently.

## 1. Scalable Folder Structure
We will adopt a structure that separates concerns:
```
ai_knowledge_hub/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py          # Entry point
│   ├── models.py        # Database tables (SQLAlchemy)
│   ├── schemas.py       # Pydantic models (Validation)
│   ├── database.py      # Database connection
│   └── routers/         # API endpoints grouped by feature
├── requirements.txt
└── .env                 # Environment variables (DB credentials)
```

## 2. SQLAlchemy & PostgreSQL
We will use **SQLAlchemy** as our ORM (Object Relational Mapper). It allows us to interact with the database using Python classes instead of writing raw SQL.

**Key Concepts:**
-   **Engine**: The entry point to the database.
-   **Session**: A temporary workspace for your operations (add, delete, query).
-   **Base**: A class that all our database models will inherit from.

## 3. Defining Models ([models.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py))
Database models represent tables in our database.

```python
from sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, String, Boolean, ForeignKey
from .database import Base

class User(Base):
    __tablename__ = "users"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    email = Column(String, unique=True, index=True)
    hashed_password = Column(String)
    is_active = Column(Boolean, default=True)

class Document(Base):
    __tablename__ = "documents"
    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, index=True)
    title = Column(String, index=True)
    content = Column(String)
    owner_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey("users.id"))
```

## 4. Understanding the Code Structure

### [app/database.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/database.py)
This file handles the database connection.
-   **`create_engine`**: Opens the connection to the database.
-   **`SessionLocal`**: A factory that creates new database sessions. Each request will get its own session.
-   **[Base](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/schemas.py#4-9)**: A class that our models inherit from, so SQLAlchemy knows they are tables.

### [app/models.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py)
Defines the **Database Tables**.
-   **[User](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py#5-14)**: Has `id`, `email`, `hashed_password`.
-   **[Document](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py#15-24)**: Has `title`, `content`, and an `owner_id` which links to the [User](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py#5-14) table (Foreign Key).
-   **`relationship`**: Allows us to access related data easily (e.g., `user.documents` gives a list of all documents for that user).

### [app/schemas.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/schemas.py)
Defines the **Pydantic Models** (Data Validation).
-   **[DocumentBase](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/schemas.py#4-9)**: Common fields for creating and reading.
-   **[DocumentCreate](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/schemas.py#10-12)**: Fields required when *creating* a document.
-   **[Document](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/models.py#15-24)**: The full object returned to the user (includes `id` and `owner_id`).
-   **[Config](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/schemas.py#17-19)**: `from_attributes = True` tells Pydantic to read data from SQLAlchemy models (which are objects, not dicts).

### [app/main.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/main.py)
The entry point.
-   **`models.Base.metadata.create_all`**: Automatically creates the tables in the database if they don't exist.
-   **[get_db()](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/main.py#11-17)**: A helper function (dependency) that gives us a database session and closes it automatically when the request is done.

## 5. Switching to PostgreSQL
To use PostgreSQL, we need to:
1.  **Install the driver**: `pip install psycopg2-binary` (We did this).
2.  **Update [database.py](file:///c:/Users/sijan/OneDrive/Desktop/ai_knowledge_hub/app/database.py)**: Change the connection URL.

**Connection URL Format:**
`postgresql://<username>:<password>@<host>/<database_name>`

**Example:**
`postgresql://postgres:mypassword@localhost/ai_knowledge_hub`

